      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Crown Copyright © 2017. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Osteoblastoma is benign bone forming tumour with rare malignant transformation. The common locations include spine, proximal humerus and hip. It rarely affects the talus. A case of osteoblastoma of the talus in a 33-years old healthy male who presented to the foot and ankle clinic in October 2015 complaining of pain of the right ankle for 12 months following football injury is discussed."
      },
